    <!-- ── Suggested (not built yet) ─────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <string name="screens_suggested_heading">Community lists aren\'t here yet</string>
    <string name="screens_suggested_status">Planned for a later version. Until then, this screen stays empty.</string>
    <string name="screens_suggested_what_title">What it will do</string>
    <string name="screens_suggested_what_body">You\'ll be able to subscribe to community-reviewed lists of accounts that showed an on-screen Ad, Promoted or Shop label. Each entry lands here for you to review: the handle, its tags and the evidence. Then you dismiss it or tap Block.</string>
    <string name="screens_suggested_human_title">Every block is still yours</string>
    <string name="screens_suggested_human_body">Nothing is blocked automatically. Each block needs your tap, runs the same verified flow, and counts against the same rate limit as every other action (Settings → Blocking). Accounts you marked as a false positive or already blocked are left out.</string>
    <string name="screens_suggested_network_title">Nothing is fetched today</string>
    <string name="screens_suggested_network_body">This version makes no network requests for lists. When lists arrive, fetching will only happen when you tap, from a list pinned to a release and checked against its hash.</string>
    <string name="screens_suggested_rules_title">What lists may contain</string>
    <string name="screens_suggested_rules_body">Objective evidence only: the on-screen label shown together with the handle. Subjective categories go in separate opt-in lists. Entries expire after 12 months unless re-confirmed, and creators can appeal.</string>
    <string name="screens_suggested_more_title">Read more</string>
    <string name="screens_suggested_more_body">See FeedClean\'s project page for updates on community lists.</string>
